WEBVTT

00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:02.570
Come out, Gagaga Girl!

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:04.690
Gagaga!

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.270
Here goes!

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.000
Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:10.150
Shingetsu!

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.680
Yuma-<i>kun</i>! It's terrible! Really terrible!

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:13.420
Hey!

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.590
Listen, just come with me!

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.620
You damn tree sparrow girl!

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.750
What gives, you monster cat feline wannabe!

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:24.870
That's right!

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.580
What the hell's your problem?!

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.500
Cut it out!

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:28.340
Hmph!

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.080
What the heck're you two doing?!

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.760
What's wrong? What in the world happened?!

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:36.220
Well, we were all just talking earlier...

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.390
<i>Mascot girl?</i>

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.270
<i>That's right! I think it'd be for the best if the Numbers Club picked up a mascot girl!</i>

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.010
<i>Oh, that's not a bad idea!</i>

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.690
<i>But who should do it?</i>

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.840
<i>Don't you think Kotori-</i>san<i> would be best?</i>

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:51.690
<i>Huh?! Me?!</i>

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:56.110
<i>After all, you've witnessed the Numbers in action more than anyone else here, right?</i>

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.290
<i>Besides, you seem to be Yuma-</i>kun<i>'s girlfriend!</i>

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:03.330
<i>No way... I'm not Yuma's girlfriend or anything like that...</i>

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.250
<i>Although...</i>

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.250
<i>Are you even able to Duel, Kotori-</i>san<i>...?</i>

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:10.380
<i>That's right, cat!</i>

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:15.470
<i>No meowy is the Numbers Club's
 mascot girl gonna be unable to Duel!</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:17.930
*Ka...ching*!

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:21.890
<i>In that case, I guess Cathy-san over here, who's skilled at Dueling, is the better choice!</i>

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.640
<i>Okay~!</i>

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:25.140
<i>Wait just a minute!</i>

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.770
<i>Why pick you just because you're able to Duel, you monster cat feline wannabe?!</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:31.270
<i>*Ka-ching*...</i>

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.860
And there you have it.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.740
Because you went and said all those unnecessary things!

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:41.240
But it's for the best.

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:42.990
Hey, Kotori!

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:44.600
Keep your mouth shut, Yuma!

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:45.670
Cat-<i>chan</i>!

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:47.200
This has meow-thing to do with you, Yuma!

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.260
For goodness sakes...

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:49.700
What's the matter, everyone?

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.890
Why are you all hanging around each other at this hour?

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.190
R-R-Rio-<i>san</i>!

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:58.180
I know! Why don't we just have Rio-<i>san</i> be the mascot girl?

00:01:58.710 --> 00:01:59.340
Hold it!

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:03.350
Why should we make that Shark double girl into our mascot?!

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:05.390
Double?

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:09.690
If you're trying to pick a fight with me, you've just bought one!

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:13.230
Gosh! Tetsuo-<i>kun</i> said something he shouldn't have!

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.680
This is clearly...

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:17.220
Tetsuo and Rio-<i>san</i> are like Beauty and the Beast, or not!

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:18.830
Wh-What'd you just say?!

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:19.970
Hey, Tetsuo...!

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:23.090
Hey! Stop this! Stop it, already!

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.220
Kotori and Cat-<i>chan</i>, you both need to calm down!

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.800
This guy may have just given me a good chance.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.440
Are you sure about this, Yuma?

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:39.730
Just leave them be.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:42.440
It's natural for close friends to fight once in a while, isn't it?

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:43.470
Even so…

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:46.430
They'll make up by tomorrow and it'll be as if it never happened!

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:49.140
Is that how it works?

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.040
But that’s not even-

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:57.440
Hmph!

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:07.700
Hmph!

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:12.080
I can't believe those guys...

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:16.880
Hey, Shark Sister! Listen here...

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.960
Do you have business with me?!

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:21.700
No... Um... You see...

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:25.730
What is the deal? They all went home so quickly...

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.830
Now I can't Duel anyone...

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:29.600
In that case, I'll be your opponent.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:31.180
<i>You</i> will?

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:33.650
It's for the best.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.830
Hey, Yuma Tsukumo!

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.930
Wh-Who are you?!

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:44.570
Yuma Tsukumo, Duel against me!

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.480
<i>It's just beginning now</i>

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:57.450
<i>This story continues to be etched into my heart endlessly</i>

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.160
<i>These feelings... burning up inside!</i>

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.510
<i>Preparations for the fight are ready</i>

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:15.590
<i>I can already hear the shivering of my heart</i>

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:20.100
<i>Been waiting this whole time</i>

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.470
<i>I may meet with defeat...</i>

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:25.690
<i>But that's exactly why I have to stand back up</i>

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:30.230
<i>Need to get stronger again</i>

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.360
<i>It's good to believe</i>

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:35.070
<i>The "now", more than ever before, is</i>

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:37.530
<i>but another limit to break down</i>

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:40.580
<i>I can cross with ease</i>

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:43.040
<i>It's just beginning now</i>

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:49.080
<i>This story continues to be etched into my heart endlessly</i>

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.840
<i>These feelings... burning up inside!</i>

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.300
<i>Right here in my hand,</i>

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:58.010
<i>I'm holding a powerful trump card.</i>

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:07.060
<i>With an unbreakable heart, I face toward my dream!</i>

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:19.710
Sports Duel Tournament?

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:25.470
A Sports Duel is the only way to solve your current issues!

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:29.260
"Kotori Chaos Xyz Changes!?
 The Tumultuous Sports Duel Tournament"

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:29.300
You can repair the bonds between your friends through a hard flowing sweat!

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.270
Now I see. How about it?

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:34.230
A Sports Duel, huh?!

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:36.520
But there is one very important thing!

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.440
Yuma, if you happen to be
 the last one remaining in the Finals,

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.150
you'll have to surrender to your opponent!

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:42.980
Huh?

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:46.150
Because your objective is to make peace with everyone!

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:50.530
If you let your friends win, your bonds with them will only deepen!

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:53.080
You say some nice things!

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.330
Uh, but why are you even helping me with this?

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:59.380
Eh? Well, you see...

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:02.300
Ah, that's it! I'm your fan! Your <i>biggest</i> fan!

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:05.260
Oh, really...?

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:10.720
In that case, we'll have a Sports Duel Tournament with everyone this Sunday!

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.640
Okay, Shingetsu, let's go to all their houses and let them know!

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:14.600
Oh, sure!

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:24.030
Hey, Gilag, what are you plotting?

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:29.280
Alit, I came up with a brilliant plan!

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:32.410
I have no idea what you're cooking up...

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.160
But I'm gonna be the one to finish Yuma Tsukumo!

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.670
Heh, do whatever you like.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:43.040
<i>Now his Numbers will belong to me...</i>

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:53.550
Now then, we shall now begin the first ever Heartland City Sports Duel Tournament!

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:56.810
Okay! Go for it, everyone!

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.520
It's for the best!

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.100
I'm not really interested, though...

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.270
Or not...

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.900
If it's a fight you want, I don't plan on losing!

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.320
Why am I here, too...?

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:16.240
Well, guys, just forget about all that and enjoy the day!

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.200
Well then, I'll announce the rules.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:20.830
We'll play sports while Tag Dueling,

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:23.630
with the winning pair earning one point each time.

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:25.960
The strongest two teams will advance to the Finals!

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:28.210
I will now pair you all up.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.170
The Yuma/Shark Team!

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:32.840
The Class Rep/Tokunosuke Team!

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.300
The Tetsuo/Rio team!

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.680
The Cat-<i>chan</i>/Kotori Team!

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.850
What's up with these pairings?!

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.440
Meowhy am I with Kotori?!

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.400
I'm happy with mine.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:45.440
Now, now, everyone.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:49.860
Whoever wins will be given the right to become the Numbers Club mascot girl!

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.150
Hey~!

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:53.740
Cat!

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:59.160
First and foremost, we shall decide the fields!

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:02.420
The first event will be... this!

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:04.080
Sky Diving!

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:15.760
Now! The first match will be a 
Skydiving Duel taking place in the sky!

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.180
Go, Aero Shark!

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.770
Good going, Shark!

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:33.110
And the first match goes to
 the Yuma/Shark Team in a beautiful victory!

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:38.700
We now switch fields! Next up is the Beach Volleyball Field!

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.200
Here I go, Tetsuo-<i>kun</i>!

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:41.910
Right!

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:46.630
I'll take care of it!

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:50.130
<i>Rio-san, watch me closely!</i>

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.550
I'll send that counter right back at you!

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:04.350
Tetsuo-<i>kun</i> makes a grave mistake!

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:11.230
Move!

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:16.860
Why'd you get in my way?!

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.240
That's my line, meow!

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:21.330
Whoa, there appears to be a quarrel among teammates.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.410
That's certainly not good.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:26.960
Just this moment, the Yuma/Shark Team has dominated the top!

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.630
And the next Field is...

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:31.500
Here!

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.720
Attack them directly!

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:39.800
Go forth, my Aurora Wing!

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.260
Trap, activate!

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:54.190
It's kinda nice to play sports once in a while.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:57.910
Yes. To summarize, it makes you forget about all the bad things.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:58.820
Or not!

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.370
Sorry that I dragged you down.

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:09.170
That's not true, you know.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:10.290
You two.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:15.920
That was a nice play. I'd like to Duel with you again sometime.

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:17.010
Sure!

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.680
I'd be glad to, meow!

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:22.470
Yuma-<i>kun</i>, our plan to make everyone get along is working great!

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:26.270
Yeah! Man! That sure was a lot of trouble!

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:26.930
Trouble?

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:27.640
Huh?

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:31.810
Weren't you just Dueling carefree like always?

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:33.110
Sh-Shut up!

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:38.900
Now then, everyone, let me announce the winning pair that will advance to the Finals!

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:41.410
The pairing with the most points is the Yuma/Shark Team!

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:42.700
Heck yeah!

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:46.910
And their match up will be none other than the Dark Horses, the Cat-<i>chan</i>/Kotori Team!

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.000
Eh?!

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:50.330
B-But why?

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:52.840
Me and Rio-<i>san</i> had more points than them!

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:56.760
All teams with two young girls gain one bonus point each!

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.590
Okay then, Kotori-<i>san</i>, Cat-<i>chan</i>.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:04.260
When we're all done here, please come with me.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:05.890
- Okay!
 - Okay!

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.570
What did you need with us?

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:18.530
Surely he's gonna give us a rare card, meow!

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:25.030
That's exactly it. I have a card right here I'd like you both to use.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.960
All for the Barian World.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:39.470
Now my preparations are flawless!

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:43.930
Now all Yuma has to do is
 lose on purpose and all his Numbers...

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:51.640
We will now begin the Tournament Finals!

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:55.150
And the field of the Finals will be... this!

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:03.990
Baseball Dueling!

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:07.200
And now, our players may enter!

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:09.500
<i>The Cat-</i>chan<i>/Kotori Team!</i>

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:14.630
And facing them are our school's strongest Duelists!

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.250
The Yuma/Shark Team!

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:19.170
Heck yeah! Let's do this!

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:20.210
Yuma! Yuma!

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:21.050
Huh?

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:25.180
You understand, don't you?
 You have to lose this Final Match on purpose.

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:25.760
Hmm?

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:31.390
It's so you can raise the bonds between those two girls even more!

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:32.270
Oh...

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:35.770
Okay! I get it!

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:37.440
Now then, Ryouga-<i>kun</i>...

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:40.990
Huh? Huh?! Uh, Ryouga-<i>kun</i>?!

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:43.110
Where'd Ryouga-<i>kun</i> go?!

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.240
I'm so sorry!

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.950
My brother went home already.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:50.200
To summarize, he basically said,
 "Like hell I'll do something like this!"

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.040
N-No way...

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.710
Can't help him!

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:59.000
Then I guess that just means 
you'll have to be our pinch hitter!

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:03.510
Eh?! Me?! Wait just a minute! I can't, uh...

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:04.970
Eh?! What's with this getup?!

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:08.640
Well, here I go! Duel Disk, set!

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:15.310
Hold it! Hold it! Ahhh!

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:16.560
Duel!!

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:23.440
<i>Wait just a minute. 
Those girls have Chaos Xyz's, don't they?</i>

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:26.110
<i>And Yuma's gonna lose on purpose, isn't he?</i>

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:28.780
<i>And if that happens, Astral's gonna disappear, right?</i>

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:32.700
<i>And doesn't that mean I'll also disappear along with him?!</i>

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.160
I'm going first!

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:37.210
My turn! Draw!

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:40.960
Yuma, do you really plan to lose on purpose?

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:44.170
Yup. If I'm gonna lose on purpose...

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:46.010
Uh, um, Yuma-<i>kun</i>...

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:48.390
I Summon Needle Swordsman!

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:55.390
I then set a card and end my turn!

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:55.930
Uh...

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:58.810
<i>This idiot! Playing such a weak Monster...</i>

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:02.980
My turn! Draw!

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:05.860
I Summon Cat Girl!

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:10.450
Meow! Cat!

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:14.750
I attack Needle Swordsman with Cat Girl!

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:17.960
Meow! Cat!

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.300
<i>Not good! This is not good at all!</i>

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:28.510
How about it, Yuma-<i>kun</i>?

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:31.300
How about we try taking this fight seriously instead?

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:34.720
Then our plan to have them make up will be a huge failure!

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:37.980
I'll show them a flashy loss!

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:40.650
<i>Oh crap! Oh crap!</i>

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:44.570
<i>If they activate Barian's Force, I'll...</i>

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:49.570
<i>That's it! I just have to destroy it before it activates!</i>

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:52.120
My turn! Draw!

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:54.870
I Summon Magic Hand!

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:03.500
I then set two cards. Turn end!

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:05.800
My turn! Dra-

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:06.800
Hold off on that draw!

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:09.430
Trap, activate! Magic Search!

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:17.220
Instead of drawing, this card lets the opponent add one Magic Card from their deck to their hand.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:23.020
<i>With this, she is certain to
 have added Barian's Force to her hand.</i>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.440
Then I activate Magic Hand's effect!

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:31.450
If the opponent adds a card from their deck to their hands that happens to be a Magic Card,

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:35.120
that card is destroyed and you take 800 points of damage!

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.870
<i>Now I can destroy Barian's Force!</i>

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:40.120
Man, no helping it.

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:42.830
You may as well go and use my Trap Card.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.590
Eh?! You're gonna help me out?!

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:47.090
Of course I am.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:50.470
Then I'll borrow your strength! Trap Card, Forgetfulness!

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:54.180
When a Monster on the field activates its effect,

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:57.560
that Monster's switched to
 Defense Position and its effect is negated!

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:05.310
<i>He just wasted my Monster Effect!</i>

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:08.980
That's no good! You're not supposed to try to beat them!

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:13.530
I Summon Little Fairy!

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:22.080
I then activate this Monster's effect!

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:24.500
I send one card from my hand to the Graveyard...

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.210
And I raise this Monster's level by one!

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:32.340
Now they have two Level Four Monsters!

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:33.470
Is she gonna do it?

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:35.220
No, stop it!

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:39.060
I Overlay the Level Four Cat Girl and Little Fairy!

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:42.520
Xyz Summon!

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:46.770
Appear now, Fairy Cheer Girl!

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:49.940
Go-go!

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.450
Whoa! That's amazing, Kotori!

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:55.820
Kotori-<i>san</i>'s really doing well.

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:57.910
Maybe she's just been playing
 the friendly girl up until now, or not...

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.740
Something's not right.

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:00.620
Huh?

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:03.790
The atmosphere around those two
 seems different from the usual...

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:06.500
Could this be...?!

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:09.460
I activate Fairy Cheer Girl's effect!

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.670
I can detach an Overlay Unit once per turn,

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:14.760
and draw one card!

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:21.270
Oh crap, oh crap! I'm gonna disappear!

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:26.600
Could this be...?!

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:31.900
Take this!

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:34.700
I activate the Rank Up Magic, Barian's Force!

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:36.110
Wh-What?!

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:41.160
I'm done for!

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:45.120
This card raises the rank of one Xyz Monster by one,

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:46.920
and changes it into an Chaos Xyz!

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:51.170
I use Fairy Cheer Girl to rebuild the Overlay Network!

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:58.010
Chaos Xyz Change!

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:02.810
Now is the time to appear! Become a symbol of the great power of Barian!

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:07.640
Chaos Xyz: Dark Fairy Cheer Girl!

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:16.610
What the heck is going on here?

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:18.660
Why are Kotori and Cat-<i>chan</i> being controlled by Barian?!

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:22.200
It's all over!

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:25.330
Dark Fairy, attack Magic Hand!

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:27.750
Fairy Turn Particle!

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:35.590
I use this moment to activate Dark Fairy's effect!

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:39.180
When the opponent's Monster is destroyed in battle,

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:41.430
I can detach one Chaos Overlay Unit...

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:47.480
...and deal 500 points of damage for each card I hold in my hand!

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.770
I have four in my hand!

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:53.230
Thus, you'll each take 2000 damage!

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:02.160
Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:05.950
Darn it! I can't believe they're both being controlled by Barian!

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.920
It's no use... I'm gonna lose it to 'em!

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:11.790
Yuma.

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:16.300
If we want to save Kotori and Cathy, we need to win this Duel.

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:19.420
Yeah! We can't keep losing on purpose!

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:21.550
My turn! Draw!

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:23.970
This is...

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:25.180
Yuma.

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:26.930
We've got our formula for victory ready.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:27.520
Yeah!

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:30.100
I Summon Gagaga Girl!

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:33.770
Gagaga!

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:37.190
And then I activate the Magic Card, Level Meister!

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:41.450
This card lets me send a card in my hand to the Graveyard

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:46.870
and changes the level of a Monster on the field by the level of the Monster sent to the Graveyard!

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:50.370
I raise Gagaga Girl's level from three to four!

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:54.130
And then I activate the Magic Card, Resurrection of the Dead!

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:55.920
Revive, Gagaga Magician!

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:02.800
I Overlay the Level Four Gagaga Magician and Gagaga Girl!

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:04.550
Xyz Summon!

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:10.930
Show yourself, our pinch hitter! 
Number 39, Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:16.150
Hope's only got 2500 Attack Points!

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:17.900
Even if you attack, they'll just destroy each other!

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:22.360
I activate the effect of Gagaga Girl, who's become Xyz Material!

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:25.320
She can make the Attack Power of one of the opponent's Xyz Monsters zero!

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:27.200
Zero Zero Call!

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:34.080
Yuma, use my Trap, Hand Power!

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:34.540
Okay!

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:37.340
Trap, activate! Hand Power!

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:42.800
Now I see. With this card, you can Banish one "Hand" Monster from your Graveyard,

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:45.550
and double the Attack Power of a Monster you control.

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:48.010
I Banish Magic Hand from the Graveyard!

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:51.600
Now Hope's Attack Power is doubled!

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:54.440
Go, Hope!

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:05.740
Hope Sword! Bases Loaded! Home Run!

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:21.300
Yes!

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:22.630
You did it, Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:25.090
I-I'm saved~!

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:27.550
I'm saved, darn it~!

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:30.560
Hey, are you two all right? Hey...

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:32.390
Huh...? Yuma?

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:37.150
What were we... doing?

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:38.690
My cat memory...

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:45.150
Then you two really don't remember this Duel at all?

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:48.740
Now let's settle the score!

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:50.120
Darling, let's Duel!

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:51.870
Gimme a break already!

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:53.660
- Wait!
 - Wait!

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:55.370
You guys can't even win the tournament now!

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:55.790
What's that mean?!

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:59.880
Yuma Tsukumo, you saved me today, but I won't forget this!

00:22:01.340 --> 00:22:07.720
I'm telling you I've had more than enough of your Duels!

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:24.190
<i>Does the thought "In any case..." following</i>

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:31.870
<i>the foreboding premonition tell you to give up?</i>

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:39.460
<i>Do you laugh at your dreams, saying "impossible"?</i>

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:46.800
<i>You must find it funny that I'm not able to laugh at it, right?</i>

00:22:47.340 --> 00:23:03.730
<i>This song supports me, so I'll do my best for you this time.
 It's my turn to sing now.</i>

00:23:03.730 --> 00:23:08.530
<i>I will vow to you here</i>

00:23:08.530 --> 00:23:18.870
<i>As long as I live, you'll always be my tiny, little friend</i>

00:23:18.870 --> 00:23:27.420
<i>I'll erase all those little mistakes of yours</i>

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:32.220
<i>Because I want to become an artist</i>

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:38.520
<i>Look, I like doing it 'cuz it's fun.</i>

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:45.320
In order to learn how to oppose the Chaos Xyz's, Yuma and Kotori visit Rokujuro's dojo.

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:48.690
Trying to forget about the fighting briefly, the two attempt to rest their minds.

00:23:48.690 --> 00:23:53.450
But suddenly, the Sphere Field manifests in the sky and a new enemy appears!

00:23:54.530 --> 00:23:56.200
So they plan to go this far?!

00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:59.200
It's time to use the power the old man gave us!

00:23:59.200 --> 00:24:00.960
What in the world is that dragon?!

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:03.170
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:03.170 --> 00:24:07.000
"The Lone Barian Knight:
 Misael the Galaxy-Eyes Master Appears"

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:09.010
He's got Number 107?!
